he wake of the European Economic Community's formation, EFTA was designed to unite non-EU countries in Europe, such as Norway, Switzerland, Iceland, and Liechtenstein, fostering economic cooperation and reducing trade barriers. Its headquarters in Geneva serves as a hub for negotiations and the development of trade agreements, making it a crucial player in global commerce.

